  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a persistent dry cough, palpitations, slow recovery from infections, and intermittent sore throat. These symptoms collectively point toward a lower respiratory tract condition. A lingering cough combined with tachycardia (palpitations) and prolonged illness duration is highly characteristic of pneumonia, where systemic inflammation and increased work of breathing elevate heart rate. Other options like bronchial asthma typically feature wheezing and episodic breathlessness, while the common cold is acute and self-limiting. The clinical picture aligns best with pneumonia.",
